class:: PipeWirePatch
summary:: Route a SuperCollider server's PipeWire client to other nodes on the graph
categories:: External Control>PipeWire
related:: Classes/PipeWire, Classes/PipeWirePort, Classes/PipeWireLink, Classes/Server

description::

A convenience wrapper around link::Classes/PipeWire:: bound to one
link::Classes/Server::'s PipeWire client. It locates that server's playback and
capture nodes and lets you connect/disconnect them to other clients on the
PipeWire graph.

This pairs with the local experimental native PipeWire backend for scsynth
(strong::-DAUDIOAPI=pipewire::), which names each server's nodes
code::"<clientName> playback":: / code::"<clientName> capture":: and groups them
under code::application.name = <clientName>::. The client name comes from
link::Classes/ServerOptions#-device::. Give each server a distinct device string
and you can target several servers independently.

subsection:: Requirements

list::
## code::pw-link:: on PATH (from the emphasis::pipewire:: / emphasis::pipewire-utils:: package).
## scsynth built with the experimental PipeWire backend.
::

subsection:: Naming

Set the client name strong::before:: booting:

code::
s.options.device = "scMain";   // names the nodes "scMain playback" / "scMain capture"
s.boot;
::

A bare device string is the client name (JACK-style); a string of the form
code::"name:target":: also targets a specific sink/source. See the backend's
strong::-H:: documentation.

ClassMethods::

method:: new
Create a patch bound to a server (or a bare client-name string).

argument:: server
A link::Classes/Server:: (the client name is derived from its
link::Classes/ServerOptions#-device::), or a link::Classes/String:: used
directly as the client name. Defaults to link::Classes/Server#*default::.

returns:: a PipeWirePatch.

InstanceMethods::

subsection:: Information

method:: server
The bound link::Classes/Server::, or code::nil:: if constructed from a name string.

method:: clientName
The PipeWire client name (the code::application.name:: of both nodes).

method:: outNodeName
method:: inNodeName
The code::node.name:: of the playback / capture node
(code::"<clientName> playback":: / code::"<clientName> capture"::).

method:: outputs
The server's output ports (its DSP outputs), in channel order.
returns:: an Array of link::Classes/PipeWirePort::. code::outputs[0]:: is channel 0.

method:: inputs
The server's capture input ports (its DSP inputs), in channel order.
returns:: an Array of link::Classes/PipeWirePort::.

method:: monitors
The capture node's monitor output ports (a copy of what was captured).
returns:: an Array of link::Classes/PipeWirePort::.

method:: numOutputs
method:: numInputs
The number of output / input channels (code::== outputs.size:: / code::inputs.size::).
returns:: an link::Classes/Integer::.

method:: links
All links touching either of this client's nodes.
returns:: an Array of link::Classes/PipeWireLink::.

method:: report
Post a readable summary (nodes, ports, links) to the post window.

subsection:: Bulk routing

All routing methods block until pw-link returns.

method:: connectOutputsTo
Connect this server's outputs to a destination's inputs, pairing ports in channel
order (the destination wraps if it has fewer ports).

argument:: target
A node-name link::Classes/String::, a link::Classes/Server::, a PipeWirePatch, a
link::Classes/PipeWirePort::, or an link::Classes/Array:: of any of those.

returns:: the number of links made (an link::Classes/Integer::).

method:: connectInputsFrom
Connect a source's outputs into this server's capture inputs (paired in channel order).

argument:: source
A node-name link::Classes/String::, link::Classes/Server::, PipeWirePatch,
link::Classes/PipeWirePort::, or link::Classes/Array:: thereof.

returns:: an link::Classes/Integer::.

method:: disconnectOutputs
method:: disconnectInputs
Remove all links from this client's output ports / into its input ports.
returns:: the number of links removed.

method:: disconnectAll
Remove every link touching either node.
returns:: the number of links removed.

subsection:: Single port-to-port routing (by channel index)

method:: connectOutput
Connect this server's output channel code::srcIndex:: to a single input channel
of code::target::.

argument:: srcIndex
The output channel index on this server.
argument:: target
The destination (same types as link::#-connectOutputsTo::).
argument:: dstIndex
The input channel index on the destination. Defaults to code::srcIndex::.
returns:: a link::Classes/Boolean:: (false, with a warning, if an index is out of range).

method:: connectInput
Connect a single output channel of code::source:: into this server's input
channel code::dstIndex::.

argument:: dstIndex
The input channel index on this server.
argument:: source
The source (same types as link::#-connectInputsFrom::).
argument:: srcIndex
The output channel index on the source. Defaults to code::dstIndex::.
returns:: a link::Classes/Boolean::.

method:: disconnectOutput
argument:: srcIndex
argument:: target
argument:: dstIndex
Remove the single link our output code::srcIndex:: -> code::target:: input
code::dstIndex:: (defaults to code::srcIndex::).
returns:: a link::Classes/Boolean::.

method:: disconnectInput
argument:: dstIndex
argument:: source
argument:: srcIndex
Remove the single link code::source:: output code::srcIndex:: (defaults to
code::dstIndex::) -> our input code::dstIndex::.
returns:: a link::Classes/Boolean::.

Examples::

subsection:: Inspect

code::
s.options.device = "scMain";
s.boot;

p = PipeWirePatch(s);
p.report;                       // nodes, ports, links

p.numOutputs;                   // 2 (or whatever -o was)
p.outputs;                      // [ PipeWirePort(...output_AUX0...), ... ]
p.outputs[0].fullName;          // "scMain playback:output_AUX0"
p.inputs;                       // capture input ports
p.links;                        // links touching scMain
::

subsection:: Connect to a hardware sink/source

code::
// Find a sink/source node name (see also PipeWire.nodes):
~sink = PipeWire.inPorts.detect { |x| x.node.contains("pro-output") }.node;
~src  = PipeWire.outPorts.detect { |x| x.node.contains("pro-input") }.node;

// How many channels does the sink expose?
PipeWire.inPortsOf(~sink).size;

// Bulk: all of our outputs -> the sink (channel-ordered):
p.connectOutputsTo(~sink);
p.connectInputsFrom(~src);

// Tear down:
p.disconnectOutputs;
p.disconnectAll;
::

subsection:: Single channels by index

code::
// our output 0 -> sink input 1
p.connectOutput(0, ~sink, 1);
// our output 1 -> sink input 3
p.connectOutput(1, ~sink, 3);
// source output 2 -> our input 0
p.connectInput(0, ~src, 2);

// remove a specific pair:
p.disconnectOutput(0, ~sink, 1);
::

subsection:: Patch one server into another (multiple servers)

code::
// Two servers with distinct names:
~a = Server(\a, NetAddr("127.0.0.1", 57111), ServerOptions.new.device_("scA").numOutputBusChannels_(2));
~b = Server(\b, NetAddr("127.0.0.1", 57112), ServerOptions.new.device_("scB").numInputBusChannels_(2));
~a.boot; ~b.boot;

~pa = PipeWirePatch(~a);
~pb = PipeWirePatch(~b);

// route server A's outputs into server B's capture inputs:
~pa.connectOutputsTo(~pb);          // or ~pb.connectInputsFrom(~pa)

// a single channel between them:
~pa.connectOutput(0, ~pb, 1);
::
